 "section_summary": "This section of the file opens with the conclusion of an extensive classified catalogue of Japanese books, government publications, periodicals, laws, and directories across subjects ranging from propaganda and foreign commerce to literature and fiction. Following this bibliography, State-War-Navy Coordinating Committee records establish United States policy (SWNCC 216/1) for international coordination in exploiting Japanese intelligence targets under American military command. The remaining documents comprise State Department diplomatic correspondence regarding the handling and screening of former Japanese officials' personal effects and archives in Italy and Canada, concluding with an illustrated Italian auction catalogue for the furnishings of the former Japanese Embassy at Villa Berlingieri in Rome.",
