   "summary": "State-War-Navy Coordinating Committee memorandum SWN-4570 transmits approved policy paper SWNCC 216/1, as amended by the Joint Chiefs of Staff, establishing United States policy for international coordination in exploiting Japanese intelligence targets in Japan and liberated areas. The directive authorizes CINCAFPAC and CINCPAC to coordinate intelligence requests, sharing material with Far Eastern Commission members and active wartime Allies while safeguarding sensitive information affecting United States security or technological superiority. It outlines specific administrative channels for submitting requests through military representatives, SCAP, or diplomatic channels.",
